{"paper": "SSC-MTS-Tier1-30-Oct-2024-Shift1.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 20, "tagged_count": 20, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "17.5", "added": false}, {"text": "21", "added": false}, {"text": "18.5", "added": false}, {"text": "16.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "The average of the first twelve multiples of 11 is:", "options": [{"text": "71.5", "added": false}, {"text": "70.5", "added": false}, {"text": "69.5", "added": false}, {"text": "68.5", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "By selling an article for ₹19.5, a dealer makes a profit of 10%. By how much should he increase his selling price (in ₹, rounded off to two decimal place) so as to make a profit of 30%?", "options": [{"text": "6.55", "added": false}, {"text": "3.55", "added": false}, {"text": "5.55", "added": false}, {"text": "4.55", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "The HCF of 21 and 49 is:", "options": [{"text": "7", "added": false}, {"text": "3", "added": false}, {"text": "1", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cylinder", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "S gets 78, 75, 68, 64 and 58 marks in Hindi, English, Chemistry, Physics and Mathematics, respectively. What are his average marks per subject?", "options": [{"text": "68.6", "added": false}, {"text": "68.8", "added": false}, {"text": "66.6", "added": false}, {"text": "66.8", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "What will be the average of all the odd numbers from 11 to 71 (both inclusive)?", "options": [{"text": "41", "added": false}, {"text": "47", "added": false}, {"text": "39", "added": false}, {"text": "31", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "Gagandeep marks his goods 50% above the cost price and offers a discount of 25% on the marked price to his customers. What is the percentage gain of Gagandeep?", "options": [{"text": "12.0%", "added": false}, {"text": "13.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "12.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "13.0%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "single-discount", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "A person spends 75% of his income. If his income increases by 15% and expenditure decreases by 10%, then what percentage increase will occur in his savings?", "options": [{"text": "47.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "67.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "22.5%", "added": false}, {"text": "90%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "income-expenditure", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "The difference between the selling prices with 19% profit and 11% loss is Rs.454.50. What is the cost price of the item?", "options": [{"text": "Rs.1,505", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.1,520", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.1,515", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.1,525", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "profit-loss-percent", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "26% less", "added": false}, {"text": "34% more", "added": false}, {"text": "26% more", "added": false}, {"text": "34% less", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "In a group of 200 members, 45% are teenagers and the remaining are adults. The average weight of the whole group is 62 kg. If the average weight of teenagers is 56 kg, then the nearest integral value of the average weight of adults is ________.", "options": [{"text": "67 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "84 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "65 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "79 kg", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "simple-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "The diameter of a hollow hemisphere is 40 cm. Water is filled in it up to its brim. When spherical lead shots each of diameter 0.8 cm are dropped into the hemisphere, three-fifths of the water flows out. How many lead shots were dropped into the hemisphere?", "options": [{"text": "30500", "added": false}, {"text": "35700", "added": false}, {"text": "35500", "added": false}, {"text": "37500", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "sphere-hemisphere", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "A cooperative society increases the annual rate of simple interest from 10% to 16½ %, then the yearly income of a person increases by ₹1,077.70. The simple interest (in₹) on the sum at 10% for four years will be:", "options": [{"text": "8,240", "added": false}, {"text": "16,580", "added": false}, {"text": "6,632", "added": false}, {"text": "9,120.3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-formula", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "Find the simple interest (in ₹) on ₹3000 as a sum borrowed at 5% per year rate of interest for 4 years.", "options": [{"text": "560", "added": false}, {"text": "540", "added": false}, {"text": "640", "added": false}, {"text": "600", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "rate-time-principal", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "A speed of 16 km/h is the same as:(Up to 1 place of decimal)", "options": [{"text": "8.4 m/sec", "added": false}, {"text": "2 m/sec", "added": false}, {"text": "4.4 m/sec", "added": false}, {"text": "8 m/sec", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "51,240", "added": false}, {"text": "41,360", "added": false}, {"text": "45,230", "added": false}, {"text": "48,250", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "table", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "Find the simple interest (in ₹) on ₹2500 as a sum borrowed at 5% per year rate of interest for 4 years.", "options": [{"text": "460", "added": false}, {"text": "500", "added": false}, {"text": "440", "added": false}, {"text": "540", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "rate-time-principal", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "The weight of a sphere is jointly proportional to the cube of its radius and the density of the material of which it is made. The radii of two spheres are 17 : 8 and the densities of materials 3 : 4. If the weight of the second sphere be 40 kg, then the approximate weight of the first sphere is:", "options": [{"text": "123.26 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "96 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "287.87 kg", "added": false}, {"text": "230 kg", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "If a man takes 36 minutes to cover a certain distance at a speed of 6 km/h, then the distance covered by him is:", "options": [{"text": "2 km", "added": false}, {"text": "3 km", "added": false}, {"text": "2.5 km", "added": false}, {"text": "3.6 km", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": null}]}